replace('A cardinality-aware interpolation extends the same alignment operator to small reference banks.',r'A cardinality-aware interpolation extends the operator to small banks. A natural alternative is to learn a router from pseudo-novel base classes. Our first-principles structural design instead derives the query gate from fixed references and the ridge identity, avoiding an additional routing fit to that surrogate distribution.')
replace('Experiments separate its recognition frontier from the selected policy and test source-only transfer as well as target recalibration.',r'On Pets L/14, it exceeds base-only logistic/MLP gates by 7.32/2.85 capacity points and 21.75/15.25 direct-admission points (Supplement V). After independent fusion tuning, actual-base-matched ImageNet-R capacity gains over dense prototypes are 3.35 [1.92,4.98]/17.86 [11.88,24.60] points (L/14/B/32; ten/six feasible partitions), separating recognition from selected-policy gains.')
